<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">LGT Group</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as LGT Bank</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">LGT is a private banking and asset management group owned by the princely family of Liechtenstein, which took over the Bank in Liechtenstein founded in 1920. In 2008 data stolen from its trust subsidiary exposed German tax evaders, causing a diplomatic dispute and international pressure on Liechtenstein's banking secrecy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lgt-group.jpg" alt="LGT Group" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LGT · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LGT_Logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
